WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:09.960
In 2018, Michigan State’s ex-president,
Lou Anna Simon, was forced from office

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:13.720
after the horrific Larry Nassar sexual abuse scandal.

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:17.800
Then, the university handed Simon a
sweetheart retirement deal.

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:22.820
Simon’s failure to address a documented
and long-standing pattern of criminal abuse

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:27.160
was apparently not cause enough to trim
the cords of her golden parachute.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:32.680
Unfortunately, getting a pass for being asleep at the switch seems pretty much the norm

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:35.240
when it comes to leaders at America’s colleges.

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:39.360
Recall the spring 2019 “Varsity Blues”
college admissions scandal.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:44.760
The parents and the sleaze-merchants who orchestrated
the scheme are facing serious repercussions.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:50.760
The oblivious campus mandarins who presided over the corruption? They’ve gotten off scot-free.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:55.400
It’s no wonder that polling shows
Americans on both the left and right

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:57.960
are losing faith in higher education.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:02.140
The industry's leaders demand
more and more public support.

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:05.620
The least we should expect is that these
same leaders be held accountable

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:08.060
when they betray the public trust.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:13.220
Do you think university leaders should be more accountable for what happens on their watch?

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:14.775
Let us know in our poll.

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:19.340
Also, let us know what other topics you'd like
our scholars to cover in 60 seconds

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:24.520
and be sure to like and subscribe for more
research and videos from AEI.

